      value: -452
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6715514986418929216, guid: ecb50d97091b9c54cae541f86a929a07, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.x
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6715514986418929216, guid: ecb50d97091b9c54cae541f86a929a07, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.y
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6715514986418929216, guid: ecb50d97091b9c54cae541f86a929a07, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.z
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8381803997503107674, guid: ecb50d97091b9c54cae541f86a929a07, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Rumors tell that the Yakuza boss, was actually a foreigner, a demon...\r\n\r\nMacaroni
        always felt alienated for being a foreigner, ostracized for his appearance,
        and as a son of lower-class parents who made their living selling antiques.
        Eventually, he found a mentor in the elderly Yakuza boss, who recognized
        his cleverness and ruthlessness early on.\r\n\r\nHowever, this would later
        become his biggest regret, as Macaroni usurped the throne to become the boss
        of the gang. Under his reign, the Yakuza rose in infamy, becoming a plague
        throughout the nation. Their goal is to topple the nation through enterprise
        and corruption.\r\n\r\nDeemed a threat by the emperor, Macaroni was dubbed
        the title of- \n\u201CThe Pariah Oni\u201D."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8381803997503107674, guid: ecb50d97091b9c54cae541f86a929a07, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontSize
      value: 23.75
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
